# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every script here is executed on Linux. A CR byte does not disappear harmlessly:
# it becomes part of the last word on the line, which breaks `case` labels, pattern
# matching, arithmetic and the shebang, and it makes a generated site list
# unusable because every path ends with \r. A Windows checkout of this repository
# must therefore still produce LF files.
#
# Normalise on commit, check out with LF.
*                   text=auto eol=lf

# Shell and the things a shell reads.
*.sh                text eol=lf
*.bash              text eol=lf
tests/stub/wp       text eol=lf
Makefile            text eol=lf
.editorconfig       text eol=lf

# Configuration and documentation.
*.conf              text eol=lf
*.conf.example      text eol=lf
*.example           text eol=lf
*.txt               text eol=lf
*.md                text eol=lf
LICENSE             text eol=lf

# Deployment units and CI: systemd parses the unit files on the host, and a stray
# CR in a `[Timer]` section is an error the operator sees only at enable time.
*.service           text eol=lf
*.timer             text eol=lf
*.yml               text eol=lf

# Generated at run time and must never be committed (see .gitignore). Marked -text
# so that if one is ever added by force, git does not rewrite its endings.
wp-found.txt        -text
*.log               -text
*.log.state         -text

# Binary assets, should the project ever grow one.
*.png               binary
*.jpg               binary
*.gif               binary
*.ico               binary
*.pdf               binary
*.tar.gz            binary
*.gz                binary

# Linguist: the repository is a shell project, not a documentation project.
*.md                linguist-documentation
